From 454d6a18a77bc3096848caacb7c458b3c2926b02 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ericek111 <erik.brocko@letemsvetemapplem.eu>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 19:52:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm_file_update_pid: no synchronize_rcu() for FreeBSD's
 integer pids

On FreeBSD the pid is a plain integer and task_pid() is the thread id, so every DRM ioctl from a new
thread waited a full RCU grace period for nothing: no reader can hold an integer.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DP5dwQG4pUvK6V9ftNsQRB
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/drm_file.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_file.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_file.c
index 6d25949758..3410296692 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_file.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_file.c
@@ -498,7 +498,14 @@ void drm_file_update_pid(struct drm_file *filp)
 #endif
 	mutex_unlock(&dev->filelist_mutex);
 
+	/*
+	 * FreeBSD: the pid is a plain integer (and task_pid() is the thread id,
+	 * so this runs for every new calling thread): no reader can hold the old
+	 * one, so there is no grace period to wait for.
+	 */
+#ifdef __linux__
 	synchronize_rcu();
+#endif
 	put_pid(old);
 }
 
